 * the heap.  FUN_10020ae8 sets the personality, the roles (+0x56), the
 * turns owned (+0xba) and the city flags (+0x11e) of every city, the
 * fronts' age and the battle memory, but never the unit counts (+0x182)
 * nor the pool counts (+0x1e6): a city keeps whatever the heap held until
 * its first garrison placement (FUN_10010b30) counts it.  That placement
 * compares the old count with the new one before its 1d6 (Erythea round
 * 12: side 2's city 54 was still 44, so it did not roll).
 *
 * The values (100 cities per side) were read out of the original running
 * in the devloop emulator (Mac OS 8.6, Erythea, seed 715183689) at turn 1;
 * they were the same at another launch and, for the cities never placed,
 * still there at round 12.  As with orig_unit_front_bits.inc they belong to
 * that heap, not to the game: only same-seed (FIXED_SEED) builds use them.
 */
